Upon further debugging, it seems like the offending line is actually the `Ref<StyleBox> bg` being null. (Should've read the first error message :sweat_smile:)

https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/3ddab1c9d171dc69a3ebf1ad747dfaea19e49339/scene/gui/tree.cpp#L3373-L3375

I looked at other uses of this line but there's never a check that it's valid. Yet a check for null pointer curiously **does not** crash Godot.

```c++
Ref<StyleBox> bg = cache.bg;
if (bg != nullptr)
  expand_area -= (bg->get_margin(MARGIN_LEFT) + bg->get_margin(MARGIN_RIGHT));
```

Not amazing with pointers and not sure how the ref class can help with this. Would like more information.
